#!/usr/bin/env too

psyche changelog:
  Write only CHANGELOG.md, in English, using Keep a Changelog 1.1.0.
  Use full git log messages; consult a PR description with gh only to resolve
  unclear user impact or migration. Apart from the current changelog and Git
  metadata for baseline and links, read no repository files, including AGENTS.md,
  or commit diffs. Never read or restore historical changelogs.
  Preserve existing records; prepend missing changes. Correct only verified
  factual errors or necessary migration guidance, explaining each correction.
  Summarize the range's final user impact; omit internal details and boilerplate.
  Link available PRs; each new entry uses one sentence of at most 30 words.
  Mark breaking entries **Breaking:**; use at most two sentences and 50 words
  naming the affected public interface and the required user action.
  Never recurse, commit, push, create issues or PRs, tag, or publish.

## Update the changelog or prepare a release entry.
agic update_changelog(since?: Text, version?: Text, date?: Text):
  psyches = psyche/changelog

  Read CHANGELOG.md if present. Baseline: {{since}}; version: {{version}};
  date: {{date}}. Require version and date together; validate YYYY-MM-DD.
  If that release heading, date, and links match and Unreleased is empty,
  return the no-change response without reviewing history.
  Verify the supplied baseline or use the latest release tag reachable from HEAD.
  Review full git log messages from the baseline through HEAD.
  Update Unreleased with a comparison link from baseline to HEAD; new files state the baseline.
  With release inputs, move Unreleased entries unchanged under that version and
  date; keep empty Unreleased above, linking baseline to target tag to HEAD.
  The target tag may be unpublished. If its section exists, add only missing
  changes belonging to it; preserve later releases.
  Check coverage, count new entries' words with code, and run git diff --check.
  Report changes briefly; if unchanged, reply only:
  "CHANGELOG.md is up to date. No changes made."
